x557 text "Programs and functions"
x558 puts x556 x557
x559 call close x558 
x560 call open x559 2
x561 write x560 2
x562 text "A program is a list of functions. A function is a header `fn NAME T... -> T`, then one instruction per line `ID OP ARGS`, then `ret ARG` (or `ret OP ARGS`, which names a fresh node), then `end`. Names are lowercase identifiers. Parameters are p0, p1, ... in header order. An argument is an earlier ID in the same function, a parameter, a u32 literal, true, or false. There are no forward references, no recursion, and no nested expressions."
x563 puts x561 x562
x564 call close x563 
x565 call open x564 10
x566 write x565 4
x567 write x566 2
x568 text "code"
x569 puts x567 x568
x570 call open x569 4
