x662 call close x661 
x663 call close x662 
x664 call close x663 
ret x664
end

fn sec_iter io -> io
x666 call open p0 13
x667 write x666 4
x668 write x667 1
x669 text "editing"
x670 puts x668 x669
x671 call open x670 11
x672 write x671 2
x673 text "Views and edits"
x674 puts x672 x673
x675 call close x674 
x676 call open x675 2
x677 write x676 2
x678 text "A model never sees a whole file. It asks for a view of one function: the function with a handle line on top (e0), one signature line per callee, and a program handle (g0). The program view is scoped to the target, its transitive callees and its direct callers, so it stays the same size as the program grows. The revision is a short hash of the program text; an edit written against an older revision is rejected rather than applied to code that has moved. A reply is the handle line followed by edits, one per line, as in the quick start."
x679 puts x677 x678
x680 call close x679 
x681 call open x680 10
x682 write x681 4
x683 write x682 2
x684 text "code"
x685 puts x683 x684
x686 call open x685 4
x687 call open x686 6
x688 write x687 4
x689 write x688 2
x690 text "cm"
x691 puts x689 x690
x692 write x691 2
x693 text "# a view of clamp, then a reply that fixes the upper bound\n"
x694 puts x692 x693
x695 call close x694 
x696 write x695 2
x697 text "e0 fn clamp u32 u32 u32 -> u32\nlo lt p0 p1\nhi lt p2 p0\na select lo p1 p0\nr select hi p2 a\nret r\n\n"
x698 puts x696 x697
x699 call open x698 6
x700 write x699 4
x701 write x700 2
x702 text "cm"
x703 puts x701 x702
x704 write x703 2
x705 text "# reply\n"
x706 puts x704 x705
x707 call close x706 
x708 write x707 2
x709 text "e0\nhi lt p2 a\nr select hi p2 a"
x710 puts x708 x709
x711 call close x710 
x712 call close x711 
x713 call close x712 
x714 call open x713 13
x715 write x714 4
x716 write x715 1
x717 text "diagnostics"
x718 puts x716 x717
x719 call open x718 11
x720 write x719 2
x721 text "Diagnostics"
x722 puts x720 x721
x723 call close x722 
x724 call open x723 2
x725 write x724 2
x726 text "Every rejection carries a stable code (parse, type, structure, handle, revision, limit), what was expected, what was seen, and the one fix that resolves it. The compiler never guesses: an ambiguous reply is rejected with the fix, not applied approximately."
x727 puts x725 x726
x728 call close x727 
x729 call close x728 
ret x729
end

